+<!DOCTYPE html>
+<html lang="en">
+<head>
+<meta charset="UTF-8">
+<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
+<title>Drill 0015 — Three-Way Merge Semantics for Append-Only Logs</title>
+<style>
+@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){*{transition:none!important;animation:none!important}}
+:root{
+  --bg:#0c1320;--surf:#18223a;--surf2:#22304e;--surf3:#2c3e62;
+  --accent:#60a5fa;--gold:#fcd34d;--green:#34d399;--red:#f87171;--orange:#fb923c;
+  --text:#dde5f5;--dim:#5a6a8a;--border:#243052;--code:#080e1c;
+  --mono:'Cascadia Code','Fira Mono','Consolas',monospace;
+}
+*{box-sizing:border-box;margin:0;padding:0}
+body{font-family:'Segoe UI',system-ui,sans-serif;background:var(--bg);color:var(--text);
+     font-size:15px;line-height:1.68;min-height:100vh}
+.screen{display:none;max-width:800px;margin:0 auto;padding:2rem 1.5rem 4rem}
+.screen.active{display:block}
+
+/* ── start ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
+.hd{text-align:center;margin-bottom:2.2rem}
+.lbl{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.72rem;color:var(--dim);letter-spacing:.15em;
+     text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:.4rem}
+.ttl{font-size:2rem;color:#fff;margin-bottom:.4rem}
+.sub{color:var(--accent);font-size:.95rem}
+
+.chips{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.55rem;justify-content:center;margin:1.4rem 0}
+.chip{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.8rem;padding:.35rem .85rem;
+      border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:20px;cursor:pointer;
+      background:var(--surf);color:var(--dim);user-select:none;transition:all .15s}
+.chip.on{border-color:var(--accent);color:var(--accent);background:rgba(96,165,250,.1)}
+.chip.all{border-color:var(--gold);color:var(--gold);background:rgba(252,211,77,.07)}
+.chip.all.on{border-color:var(--gold);color:var(--gold)}
+
+.smeta{text-align:center;color:var(--dim);font-size:.85rem;margin-bottom:.9rem}
+.shuf{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:.65rem;
+      margin-bottom:1.4rem;font-size:.86rem;color:var(--dim)}
+.tog{position:relative;display:inline-block;width:36px;height:20px}
+.tog input{opacity:0;width:0;height:0}
+.sl{position:absolute;inset:0;background:var(--surf2);border-radius:20px;cursor:pointer;transition:background .2s}
+.sl:before{content:'';position:absolute;width:14px;height:14px;left:3px;top:3px;
+           background:#fff;border-radius:50%;transition:transform .2s}
+input:checked+.sl{background:var(--accent)}
+input:checked+.sl:before{transform:translateX(16px)}
+
+/* ── question ───────────────────────────────────────────────── */
+.qhdr{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.8rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;flex-wrap:wrap}
+.qnum{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.78rem;color:var(--dim)}
+.pbar{flex:1;height:5px;background:var(--surf2);border-radius:3px;min-width:80px}
+.pfill{height:100%;background:var(--accent);border-radius:3px;transition:width .3s}
+.ctag{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.7rem;padding:.18rem .55rem;
+      border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:12px;color:var(--dim)}
+.ttag{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.7rem;padding:.18rem .55rem;border-radius:12px}
+.ttag.mc{background:rgba(96,165,250,.12);color:var(--accent)}
+.ttag.wr{background:rgba(251,146,60,.12);color:var(--orange)}
+
+.qtxt{font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:600;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1.1rem;line-height:1.5}
+pre.snip{background:var(--code);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:6px;
+         padding:.9rem 1.1rem;overflow-x:auto;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.82rem;
+         line-height:1.6;margin-bottom:1.1rem;display:none}
+.kw{color:#c792ea}.str{color:#c3e88d}.cm{color:#405060;font-style:italic}
+.fn{color:#82aaff}.num{color:#f78c6c}.cls{color:#ffcb6b}.at{color:#a5d6ff}
+.mk{color:#f87171;font-weight:700}.ours{color:#93c5fd}.theirs{color:#fcd34d}
+
+/* mc */
+.opts{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0}
+.opts li{background:var(--surf);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:6px;
+         padding:.55rem 1rem;margin-bottom:.45rem;cursor:pointer;user-select:none;
+         transition:border-color .15s,background .15s}
+.opts li:hover:not(.lk){border-color:var(--accent);background:rgba(96,165,250,.07)}
+.opts li:focus{outline:2px solid var(--accent);outline-offset:2px}
+.opts li.ok{border-color:var(--green);background:rgba(52,211,153,.09);color:var(--green)}
+.opts li.no{border-color:var(--red);background:rgba(248,113,113,.09);color:var(--red)}
+.opts li.lk{cursor:default}
+.mfb{margin-top:.65rem;font-size:.87rem;padding:.45rem .8rem;border-radius:4px;display:none}
+.mfb.ok{background:rgba(52,211,153,.1);color:var(--green);border:1px solid rgba(52,211,153,.28)}
+.mfb.no{background:rgba(248,113,113,.09);color:var(--red);border:1px solid rgba(248,113,113,.28)}
+
+/* written */
+textarea{width:100%;min-height:108px;background:var(--surf);border:1px solid var(--border);
+         border-radius:6px;padding:.7rem .9rem;color:var(--text);font-family:inherit;
+         font-size:.92rem;resize:vertical;line-height:1.55}
+textarea:focus{outline:2px solid var(--accent)}
+.wacts{display:flex;gap:.55rem;margin-top:.65rem;flex-wrap:wrap}
+.kwres{margin-top:.8rem;display:none}
+.tally{font-weight:700;margin-bottom:.4rem;font-size:.9rem}
+.kwchips{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.35rem;margin-bottom:.55rem}
+.kc{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.75rem;padding:.18rem .5rem;border-radius:12px}
+.kc.h{background:rgba(52,211,153,.12);color:var(--green);border:1px solid rgba(52,211,153,.28)}
+.kc.m{background:rgba(248,113,113,.1);color:var(--red);border:1px solid rgba(248,113,113,.28)}
+.knote{color:var(--dim);font-size:.78rem}
+.modans{display:none;margin-top:.8rem;background:var(--surf);border:1px solid var(--border);
+        border-radius:6px;padding:.8rem 1rem;font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.65;white-space:pre-wrap}
+.modlbl{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.7rem;color:var(--dim);text-transform:uppercase;
+        letter-spacing:.08em;margin-bottom:.35rem}
+.sr{display:none;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;flex-wrap:wrap;
+    font-size:.85rem;color:var(--dim);margin-top:.65rem}
+
+/* nav + buttons */
+.nav{display:flex;gap:.55rem;margin-top:1.5rem;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center}
+.spc{flex:1}
+.btn{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.83rem;padding:.45rem 1rem;border:1px solid transparent;
+     border-radius:5px;cursor:pointer;transition:opacity .15s;user-select:none}
+.btn:focus{outline:2px solid var(--accent);outline-offset:2px}
+.pri{background:var(--accent);color:#000}.pri:hover{opacity:.82}
+.sec{background:var(--surf2);color:var(--text);border-color:var(--border)}
+.sec:hover{border-color:var(--accent)}
+.grn{background:var(--green);color:#000}
+.gld{background:var(--gold);color:#000}
+.sm{padding:.32rem .7rem;font-size:.77rem}
+.red{background:var(--red);color:#fff}
+
+/* results */
+.rhdr{text-align:center;margin-bottom:1.8rem}
+.sbig{font-size:3.4rem;font-family:var(--mono);color:var(--accent)}
+.slbl{color:var(--dim);font-size:.88rem;margin-top:.25rem}
+.rcols{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1rem;margin:1.4rem 0}
+@media(max-width:520px){.rcols{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
+.rcard{background:var(--surf);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:7px;padding:.9rem 1.1rem}
+.rcard h3{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.78rem;color:var(--dim);
+          text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em;margin-bottom:.6rem}
+.miss{background:var(--surf2);border-radius:4px;padding:.38rem .65rem;
+      margin-bottom:.38rem;font-size:.86rem}
+.mcorr{color:var(--green);font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.8rem;display:block;margin-top:.2rem}
+</style>
+</head>
+<body>
+
+<!-- ═══════════ START ═══════════ -->
+<div id="S" class="screen active">
+<div class="hd">
+  <div class="lbl">Drill 0015 · Active Recall</div>
+  <div class="ttl">Three-Way Merge Semantics for Append-Only Logs</div>
+  <div class="sub">22 questions — merge mechanics, keep-one vs keep-both diagnosis, invariant repair, real-repo reading (24f142b / f2b6fbf), spot-the-bad-resolution</div>
+</div>
+<p style="text-align:center;color:var(--dim);font-size:.87rem;margin-bottom:1rem">Pick channels to drill, or keep All.</p>
+<div class="chips" id="chips">
+  <div class="chip all on" data-ch="all">⚡ All</div>
+  <div class="chip on" data-ch="mech">Merge mechanics</div>
+  <div class="chip on" data-ch="diag">Keep-one vs keep-both</div>
+  <div class="chip on" data-ch="repair">Invariant repair</div>
+  <div class="chip on" data-ch="repo">Real-repo reading</div>
+  <div class="chip on" data-ch="spot">Spot the bad resolution</div>
+</div>
+<p class="smeta" id="smeta">22 questions selected</p>
+<div class="shuf">
+  Shuffle
+  <label class="tog"><input type="checkbox" id="sh" checked><span class="sl"></span></label>
+</div>
+<div style="text-align:center">
+  <button class="btn pri" onclick="go()" style="font-size:1rem;padding:.65rem 2rem">Begin →</button>
+</div>
+</div>
+
+<!-- ═══════════ QUESTION ═══════════ -->
+<div id="Q" class="screen">
+<div class="qhdr">
+  <span class="qnum" id="qn">Q 1 / 22</span>
+  <div class="pbar"><div class="pfill" id="pf" style="width:0%"></div></div>
+  <span class="ctag" id="ct"></span>
+  <span class="ttag mc" id="tt">MC</span>
+</div>
+<div class="qtxt" id="qt"></div>
+<pre class="snip" id="qs"></pre>
+
+<div id="MA" style="display:none">
+  <ul class="opts" id="mo"></ul>
+  <div class="mfb" id="mf"></div>
+</div>
+
+<div id="WA" style="display:none">
+  <textarea id="wa" placeholder="Type your answer here…"></textarea>
+  <div class="wacts">
+    <button class="btn sec sm" onclick="chkW()">Check keywords</button>
+    <button class="btn sec sm" onclick="showM()">Show model answer</button>
+  </div>
+  <div class="kwres" id="kr">
+    <div class="tally" id="kt"></div>
+    <div class="kwchips" id="kc"></div>
+    <div class="knote">⚠ Keyword check is fuzzy — judge honestly against the model answer.</div>
+  </div>
+  <div class="modans" id="md"><div class="modlbl">Model answer</div><div id="mt"></div></div>
+  <div class="sr" id="sr">
+    Rate yourself:
+    <button class="btn grn sm" onclick="rate('k')">✓ Knew it</button>
+    <button class="btn red sm"  onclick="rate('r')">↺ Needs review</button>
+  </div>
+</div>
+
+<div class="nav">
+  <button class="btn sec sm" id="bp" onclick="prev()">← Prev</button>
+  <div class="spc"></div>
+  <button class="btn pri sm" id="bn" onclick="next()">Next →</button>
+  <button class="btn gld sm" id="bf" style="display:none" onclick="results()">Results</button>
+</div>
+</div>
+
+<!-- ═══════════ RESULTS ═══════════ -->
+<div id="R" class="screen">
+<div class="rhdr">
+  <div class="sbig" id="rb">—</div>
+  <div class="slbl" id="rl"></div>
+</div>
+<div class="rcols">
+  <div class="rcard"><h3>MC misses</h3><div id="rm"><em style="color:var(--dim);font-size:.86rem">None!</em></div></div>
+  <div class="rcard"><h3>Written — needs review</h3><div id="rw"><em style="color:var(--dim);font-size:.86rem">None flagged.</em></div></div>
+</div>
+<div style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;justify-content:center;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:.8rem">
+  <button class="btn sec" onclick="rev()">Review missed only</button>
+  <button class="btn pri" onclick="location.reload()">Restart</button>
+</div>
+</div>
+
+<script>
+// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+// QUESTION BANK  (22 questions — grounded in merges 24f142b & f2b6fbf)
+// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+const BANK = [
+
+// ─── CHANNEL: mech ────────────────────────────────────────────
+{id:'m1',ch:'mech',type:'w',
+ q:'Name the three inputs of a three-way merge and where each came from in tonight\'s 24f142b merge. Then state the decision rule git applies per region — including the two cases that produce a conflict.',
+ c:[{l:'base = merge-base (df5c43c, nearest common ancestor)',t:['merge-base','merge base','common ancestor','df5c43c']},
+    {l:'ours = HEAD / first parent (feature/issue-18)',t:['ours','head','first parent','feature branch','issue-18']},
+    {l:'theirs = branch merged in / second parent (origin/master)',t:['theirs','second parent','origin/master','master']},
+    {l:'one side changed → take it; both same → take; both differ same region → conflict',t:['only one','take that side','both changed','same region','conflict']},
+    {l:'both inserted at the same point (empty base) → conflict too',t:['insert','same point','same anchor','empty base','no ordering']}],
+ m:`Base: the file at the merge base — the nearest common ancestor of the two branches (git merge-base 24f142b^1 24f142b^2 = df5c43c). Ours: the file on HEAD, the branch being stood on (feature/issue-18-adc-reference-scaling, the first parent). Theirs: the file on the branch merged in (origin/master, the second parent).
+Decision rule, applied region by region using diffs of each side against the base:
+- neither side changed a region → keep it;
+- exactly one side changed it → take that side's version (this is why the base matters: it reveals WHO changed what, not just that the sides differ);
+- both sides made the identical change → take it once;
+- both sides changed the same region differently → CONFLICT;
+- both sides inserted different text at the same point (nothing at base — the append case) → CONFLICT, because git has no ordering rule for two insertions.
+Git stops only for the last two; everything else is decided silently.`
+},
+
+{id:'m2',ch:'mech',type:'mc',
+ q:'Why does an append-only log like PROGRESS.md conflict "by construction" when two branches each log a session?',
+ opts:[
+  {t:'Every writer inserts at the same append anchor — between the last shared entry and the stable tail heading — so both diffs against the base describe different insertions at the same point',c:true, w:'Correct. Same context above (end of the Drill 1 block), same context below (## Suggested Next Lessons), different inserted text: the exact both-inserted-at-one-point case git must refuse. Unlike source code, where parallel edits usually land in different functions, log appends always collide.'},
+  {t:'Markdown headings confuse the merge algorithm\'s context matching',c:false,w:'Git does not parse Markdown at all — headings are just lines. The collision comes from both insertions sharing the same surrounding context, which would be true in any format.'},
+  {t:'Log files are usually large, and large files always conflict',c:false,w:'Size is irrelevant; f2b6fbf auto-merged five inserted session blocks cleanly. What matters is whether the changed regions overlap.'},
+  {t:'Git locks append-only files so only one branch may modify them',c:false,w:'Git has no file locking and no append-only mode — "append-only" describes the team\'s discipline for the file, not a git feature.'},
+ ]
+},
+
+{id:'m3',ch:'mech',type:'mc',
+ q:'With merge.conflictStyle=diff3, the 24f142b hunk shows an EMPTY section between ||||||| and =======. What does that tell you?',
+ snip:`<span class="mk">&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt; HEAD</span>
+<span class="ours">### Session 3 (2026-07-15, overnight — issue #18) …</span>
+<span class="mk">||||||| merged common ancestors</span>
+<span class="mk">=======</span>
+<span class="theirs">### Session 3 (2026-06-28, overnight) …</span>
+<span class="mk">&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; origin/master</span>`,
+ opts:[
+  {t:'Neither side edited existing text — both PURELY INSERTED at this point; the strongest possible hint that this is a keep-both (both-sides-append) situation',c:true, w:'Correct. The middle section shows the base version of the disputed region. Empty base = nothing existed there before = two independent insertions, i.e. two new records — which diagnoses keep-both before you even read the entries.'},
+  {t:'The base commit is missing from the local repository',c:false,w:'If the base were unreachable the merge could not run at all. The section is empty because the base REGION is empty, not because the commit is absent.'},
+  {t:'The conflict is unresolvable and the merge must be aborted',c:false,w:'It is entirely resolvable — 24f142b resolved it. The empty base makes the resolution EASIER to choose, not harder.'},
+  {t:'diff3 style failed and fell back to the default two-section style',c:false,w:'The ||||||| marker is present, so diff3 rendered fine; its section just has zero lines of base content.'},
+ ]
+},
+
+{id:'m4',ch:'mech',type:'mc',
+ q:'Branch A renames a heading at line 47 of a file. Branch B appends five blocks after line 65 of the same file. What happens when they merge?',
+ opts:[
+  {t:'Clean auto-merge — the changed regions do not overlap, so git takes both changes without asking anyone',c:true, w:'Correct, and it is exactly the f2b6fbf setup: theirs renamed "Session 3" → "Session 4" (plus inserted the June entry) around line 47; ours appended Sessions 4–8 after line 65. Git combined them silently — producing a duplicate "Session 4". Clean is not the same as correct.'},
+  {t:'A conflict, because both branches modified the same file',c:false,w:'Conflicts are per-REGION, not per-file. Same file + disjoint regions = clean merge; that is the everyday case that makes git usable at all.'},
+  {t:'Git refuses to merge because one change is a rename',c:false,w:'Renaming a LINE\'s content is just an edit; git has no special handling for it. (File renames are detected separately and also merge fine.)'},
+  {t:'Branch B\'s appends are discarded because Branch A\'s change is earlier in the file',c:false,w:'Position in the file grants no priority — both non-conflicting changes are kept, which is precisely how the semantic breakage combined.'},
+ ]
+},
+
+{id:'m5',ch:'mech',type:'w',
+ q:'Mid-conflict, PROGRESS.md contains markers. Give the commands to view the base, ours, and theirs versions of the file straight from the index, and name the mechanism that makes this possible.',
+ c:[{l:'git show :1:path — base (stage 1)',t:[':1:','stage 1','stage one']},
+    {l:'git show :2:path — ours (stage 2)',t:[':2:','stage 2','stage two']},
+    {l:'git show :3:path — theirs (stage 3)',t:[':3:','stage 3','stage three']},
+    {l:'unmerged index stages hold all three blob versions during conflict',t:['index','unmerged','stages','blob','three versions']}],
+ m:`During a conflict the index holds the file in three numbered stages instead of one entry:
+- git show :1:Silmulator/docs/learning/PROGRESS.md   → stage 1, the BASE (merge-base version)
+- git show :2:Silmulator/docs/learning/PROGRESS.md   → stage 2, OURS (HEAD)
+- git show :3:Silmulator/docs/learning/PROGRESS.md   → stage 3, THEIRS (the branch being merged)
+The mechanism: an unmerged path keeps all three blobs staged simultaneously; git ls-files -u lists them. The working-tree file with markers is just a rendering of stages 2 and 3 (plus 1 under diff3) — the pristine inputs stay available in the index the whole time, which is also what mergetools read. Resolving and running git add collapses the three stages back to one.`
+},
+
+// ─── CHANNEL: diag ────────────────────────────────────────────
+{id:'d1',ch:'diag',type:'w',
+ q:'State the diagnostic question for a log-file conflict hunk, and list the evidence signals that point to keep-both versus keep-one versus regenerate.',
+ c:[{l:'ask: two records of different events, or two versions of one record?',t:['different events','same record','two versions','one record','question']},
+    {l:'keep-both: different dates / issue numbers / artifacts referenced',t:['different date','issue number','disjoint','artifact','keep both']},
+    {l:'keep-one: revision (typo fix, extra bullet) or verbatim superset',t:['revision','superset','typo','keep one','better version']},
+    {l:'regenerate: file is derived/generated output',t:['derived','generated','regenerate','lockfile','index']}],
+ m:`The question is never "ours or theirs?" — it is: are the two sides two records of DIFFERENT events, or two versions of the SAME record?
+- Keep both (ordered, renumbered): the sides cite different dates, different issue numbers, and reference different artifacts. 24f142b: 2026-06-28/lesson 0008 vs 2026-07-15/lesson 0009 — disjoint work, both true. Deleting either falsifies history, especially since the merge itself brought the other side's lesson files into the tree.
+- Keep one: same event, one side revised it (typo fixes, an added bullet, corrected link) — keep the revision; or one side's text contains the other's verbatim plus more — keep the superset.
+- Keep neither / regenerate: the file is derived output (index.html, lockfiles, generated reports). Neither side is the source of truth; resolve the sources and rerun the generator.
+Order for kept entries comes from the log's own invariant (chronological in PROGRESS.md), never from git's ours-first hunk layout.`
+},
+
+{id:'d2',ch:'diag',type:'mc',
+ q:'In the 24f142b conflict, which single fact makes keep-both not merely polite but REQUIRED for consistency?',
+ opts:[
+  {t:'The very same merge brings lessons/0008-visual-regression-testing.html into the tree — dropping master\'s log entry would leave the merged tree containing a lesson the log claims was never taught',c:true, w:'Correct. The log and the tree must agree. Master\'s Session 3 documents artifacts that arrive in this exact merge commit (the 0008 lesson, drill, goldens); a log that omits the entry contradicts the tree it sits in.'},
+  {t:'Git rejects resolutions that delete either side of a conflict hunk',c:false,w:'Git accepts ANY resolution text, including taking one side or deleting both. Correctness is entirely on the resolver — that is the point of the lesson.'},
+  {t:'The feature branch\'s entry was newer, and newer entries always win',c:false,w:'Recency decides nothing; and if it did, "winning" would mean deleting the June record — precisely the data loss keep-both avoids.'},
+  {t:'Both entries had the same session number, so both had to be kept to preserve the number',c:false,w:'The shared "Session 3" number is the INVARIANT VIOLATION keep-both must repair (by renumbering), not a reason for keeping both.'},
+ ]
+},
+
+{id:'d3',ch:'diag',type:'mc',
+ q:'Having decided to keep both Session-3 entries, what determines their order in the resolved file?',
+ opts:[
+  {t:'The log\'s own ordering invariant — chronological — so the June visual-testing entry precedes the July ADC entry, even though "ours" appeared first in the hunk',c:true, w:'Correct. Git prints ours above theirs purely because of which branch you stood on; it is presentation, not semantics. PROGRESS.md is chronological, so 2026-06-28 goes before 2026-07-15, and the July entry takes the next number (Session 4).'},
+  {t:'Hunk order — git lists ours first, so ours stays first',c:false,w:'Hunk order is an artifact of parent order. Standing on master and merging the feature branch would have flipped it while the correct resolution stayed the same.'},
+  {t:'Alphabetical order of the lesson titles',c:false,w:'Nothing in the file sorts alphabetically; its rule is chronological. A differently-ruled log (severity, alphabetical) would use ITS rule — the point is the file\'s rule outranks the tool\'s layout.'},
+  {t:'The larger entry goes first so context is established early',c:false,w:'Entry size is meaningless to ordering. Only the log\'s own invariant counts.'},
+ ]
+},
+
+{id:'d4',ch:'diag',type:'mc',
+ q:'A different conflict: ours has "fixed typo, added one bullet" on Session 2\'s entry; theirs has Session 2\'s entry untouched plus a brand-new Session 3 below it. Diagnosis?',
+ opts:[
+  {t:'No dilemma at all — these regions don\'t truly compete: keep ours\' revised Session 2 AND theirs\' new Session 3; it is a revision plus a new record, not two versions of one thing',c:true, w:'Correct. Apply the diagnosis per REGION: the Session-2 edits are a same-record revision (keep the revised one); the Session-3 block is a new event (keep it). If git presented them as one hunk, the resolution interleaves both — resolution is per-record, not per-hunk.'},
+  {t:'Keep-one: theirs, because it contains more sessions',c:false,w:'That discards ours\' typo fix and bullet. "More content" is not the superset test — theirs does NOT contain ours\' revision verbatim.'},
+  {t:'Keep-one: ours, because revisions outrank additions',c:false,w:'That deletes theirs\' entire new session. There is no rank between revisions and additions; both survive because they concern different records.'},
+  {t:'Regenerate the file from scratch',c:false,w:'PROGRESS.md is a source-of-truth log, not derived output — there is no generator to rerun. Regeneration applies to files like index.html.'},
+ ]
