+// ─── CHANNEL: repo ────────────────────────────────────────────
+{id:'p1',ch:'repo',type:'mc',
+ q:'git show 24f142b prints "Merge: 19d2688 d63bbbf" and a message containing "# Conflicts: Silmulator/docs/learning/PROGRESS.md". What exactly is that Conflicts trailer?',
+ opts:[
+  {t:'Documentation, not enforcement: git pre-fills the default merge-commit message with the paths that conflicted, and committing keeps it — a permanent record of where a human had to decide',c:true, w:'Correct. The trailer is inserted into the commit-message template at resolution time and survives only if the committer keeps it. It has no mechanical meaning, but as history it is gold: tonight it is the proof that PROGRESS.md conflicted loudly at 24f142b and (by its absence) merged silently at f2b6fbf.'},
+  {t:'A machine-readable field git uses to re-apply the resolution on future merges',c:false,w:'Nothing re-reads it. (Resolution REUSE exists, but it is git rerere, keyed on conflict content — not the commit message.)'},
+  {t:'Proof that the conflict is still unresolved inside the commit',c:false,w:'A commit cannot contain an unresolved conflict — committing requires all index stages collapsed. The trailer records that a conflict WAS resolved, not that it remains.'},
+  {t:'A list of files whose merge used the "ours" strategy',c:false,w:'It lists conflicted paths regardless of how they were resolved; strategy is not recorded there.'},
+ ]
+},
+
+{id:'p2',ch:'repo',type:'mc',
+ q:'f2b6fbf\'s commit message lists a conflict only for docs/learning/index.html — yet PROGRESS.md changed in that merge too. What is the correct reading?',
+ opts:[
+  {t:'PROGRESS.md auto-merged with no conflict — which is precisely why its result needed semantic verification, and indeed it had combined into a duplicate Session 4 before repair',c:true, w:'Correct. Absence from the trailer means git had no questions about the file, not that the file is right. The silent path is where the invariant checks earn their keep; the loud path (index.html) forces review by construction.'},
+  {t:'PROGRESS.md was not touched by either parent, so it carried over unchanged',c:false,w:'Both parents changed it (theirs inserted/renamed around line 47; ours appended after line 65) — git show f2b6fbf --stat lists it with 24 changed lines.'},
+  {t:'The trailer only has room for one path',c:false,w:'The trailer lists every conflicted path; 24f142b\'s lists PROGRESS.md. index.html appears alone because it was the only conflict.'},
+  {t:'index.html\'s conflict blocked PROGRESS.md from being merged',c:false,w:'Files merge independently; one file\'s conflict never blocks another\'s auto-merge. All non-conflicted results were staged while index.html waited for resolution.'},
+ ]
