+
+{id:'p3',ch:'repo',type:'w',
+ q:'Without checking anything out, reconstruct the 24f142b conflict\'s three inputs from the repo. Give the exact commands for: the merge base SHA, the base file, ours, theirs — and the command that replays the conflicted merge offline.',
+ c:[{l:'git merge-base 24f142b^1 24f142b^2',t:['merge-base','^1','^2']},
+    {l:'git show <sha>:path for base/ours/theirs file versions',t:['git show',':silmulator',':docs','colon','show 24f142b^1:']},
+    {l:'parent^1 = ours (feature), parent^2 = theirs (master)',t:['first parent','second parent','^1 = ours','^2 = theirs','ours','theirs']},
+    {l:'git merge-file (or merge-tree) replays the merge offline',t:['merge-file','merge-tree','--diff3','replay','reproduce']}],
+ m:`B=$(git merge-base 24f142b^1 24f142b^2)          # → df5c43c, nearest common ancestor
+git show $B:Silmulator/docs/learning/PROGRESS.md         > base.md    # BASE
+git show 24f142b^1:Silmulator/docs/learning/PROGRESS.md  > ours.md    # OURS  (first parent = feature/issue-18)
+git show 24f142b^2:Silmulator/docs/learning/PROGRESS.md  > theirs.md  # THEIRS (second parent = origin/master tip d63bbbf)
+git merge-file -p --diff3 ours.md base.md theirs.md      # replays the merge; prints the hunk with markers
+The ^1/^2 suffixes select the merge's parents: first parent is the branch that was checked out (ours), second is the branch merged in (theirs). git show SHA:path reads any file at any commit without touching the worktree. merge-file's exit status is the number of conflicts (here 1); the diff3 flag exposes the empty base section that fingerprints both-sides-append. The same replay on f2b6fbf's parents (903605b / a122eb4, base 701853d) exits 0 and reproduces the duplicate-Session-4 file — the whole case study is recoverable from plumbing alone.`
+},
+
+{id:'p4',ch:'repo',type:'mc',
+ q:'At f2b6fbf, docs/learning/index.html was absent at merge base 701853d and present on BOTH parents (43 lines on one, 54 on the other). What kind of conflict is this and what resolved it?',
+ opts:[
+  {t:'An add/add conflict — two independent creations with no base to diff against; resolved by taking neither and regenerating with .tools/build_index.py against the merged directory (result: 44 lines matching neither parent)',c:true, w:'Correct. With no base version, git can only present the two whole files. Since index.html is derived — a projection of lessons/ and drills/ — the generator is the resolution: the rebuilt file indexes the union of the merged tree, which neither side\'s version could.'},
+  {t:'A content conflict identical in kind to PROGRESS.md\'s',c:false,w:'PROGRESS.md was modify/modify with a common base version to diff against. add/add has NO base — the file did not exist at 701853d — which is why the candidates are whole files, not hunks.'},
+  {t:'A rename conflict — one side moved the file',c:false,w:'Neither side renamed anything; both CREATED docs/learning/index.html independently. That simultaneous creation is the definition of add/add.'},
+  {t:'A binary conflict, since HTML is treated as binary',c:false,w:'HTML is text to git; the two versions even diff cleanly (different doctype casing on line 1). The issue was independent creation, not encoding.'},
+ ]
+},
