+git add Silmulator/docs/learning/PROGRESS.md
+git commit`,
+ opts:[
+  {t:'It silently deletes master\'s Session-3 record; the merged tree then contains lesson 0008\'s files while the log never mentions them — a tree/log inconsistency any reviewer can spot',c:true, w:'Correct. --ours takes the feature branch\'s whole file, discarding theirs\' June entry. Both-sides-append means both sides are true — the one-keystroke resolution converts a loud conflict into silent history loss. Recovery: git show <merge>^2:path still holds theirs\' version forever.'},
+  {t:'Nothing — --ours is the standard resolution for documentation files',c:false,w:'There is no file-type convention that blesses --ours. For a both-sides-append log it is nearly always wrong, because it erases one side\'s real history.'},
+  {t:'The commands fail because --ours only works during rebase',c:false,w:'They succeed — checkout --ours/--theirs works during any merge conflict (during rebase, confusingly, the labels swap meaning). Succeeding is exactly the danger.'},
+  {t:'It leaves conflict markers in the committed file',c:false,w:'checkout --ours writes a clean (marker-free) copy of one side. The file is textually tidy — the damage is semantic: missing history, not stray markers.'},
