+{id:'s4',ch:'spot',type:'w',
+ q:'You are handed the f2b6fbf auto-merged headings list (below). Write the corrected heading sequence, name each change, and state the general principle this failure teaches.',
+ snip:`### Session 3 (2026-06-28, overnight)
+### Session 4 (2026-07-15, overnight — issue #18)
+### Session 4 (2026-07-15, overnight — issue #19)
+### Session 5 (2026-07-15, overnight — issue #20)
+### Session 6 (2026-07-15, overnight — issue #21)
+### Session 7 (2026-07-15, overnight — issue #22)
+### Session 8 (2026-07-15, overnight — issue #23)`,
+ c:[{l:'issue #19 → Session 5; #20 → 6; #21 → 7; #22 → 8; #23 → 9',t:['session 5','session 9','5','9','renumber']},
+    {l:'Sessions 3 and 4 (#18) stay as-is',t:['stay','unchanged','keep','as-is','as is']},
+    {l:'five headings changed, bodies untouched',t:['five','5 heading','bodies','only the heading','untouched']},
+    {l:'principle: textual success ≠ semantic success — verify invariants after clean merges',t:['textual','semantic','clean merge','verify','invariant','silent']}],
+ m:`Corrected sequence:
+### Session 3 (2026-06-28, overnight)                 — unchanged
+### Session 4 (2026-07-15, overnight — issue #18)     — unchanged (24f142b's renumbering honoured)
+### Session 5 (2026-07-15, overnight — issue #19)     — was 4 (the duplicate)
+### Session 6 (2026-07-15, overnight — issue #20)     — was 5
+### Session 7 (2026-07-15, overnight — issue #21)     — was 6
+### Session 8 (2026-07-15, overnight — issue #22)     — was 7
+### Session 9 (2026-07-15, overnight — issue #23)     — was 8
+Five headings renumbered (+1 each), entry bodies untouched, then assert: grep -oE '^### Session [0-9]+' | sort | uniq -d prints nothing.
+Principle: textual success is not semantic success. Git merged two individually-correct, non-overlapping changes into a file that violates its own invariants, and reported success — because the invariants live above the line level where git operates. Clean merges of shared logs must therefore be VERIFIED, not trusted: re-read the file or run its invariant assertions every time, precisely because no conflict was reported.`
+},
