+ q:'With merge.conflictStyle=diff3, the 24f142b hunk shows an EMPTY section between ||||||| and =======. What does that tell you?',
+ snip:`<span class="mk">&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt; HEAD</span>
+<span class="ours">### Session 3 (2026-07-15, overnight — issue #18) …</span>
+<span class="mk">||||||| merged common ancestors</span>
+<span class="mk">=======</span>
+<span class="theirs">### Session 3 (2026-06-28, overnight) …</span>
+<span class="mk">&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; origin/master</span>`,
+ opts:[
+  {t:'Neither side edited existing text — both PURELY INSERTED at this point; the strongest possible hint that this is a keep-both (both-sides-append) situation',c:true, w:'Correct. The middle section shows the base version of the disputed region. Empty base = nothing existed there before = two independent insertions, i.e. two new records — which diagnoses keep-both before you even read the entries.'},
+  {t:'The base commit is missing from the local repository',c:false,w:'If the base were unreachable the merge could not run at all. The section is empty because the base REGION is empty, not because the commit is absent.'},
+  {t:'The conflict is unresolvable and the merge must be aborted',c:false,w:'It is entirely resolvable — 24f142b resolved it. The empty base makes the resolution EASIER to choose, not harder.'},
