+{id:'m5',ch:'mech',type:'w',
+ q:'Mid-conflict, PROGRESS.md contains markers. Give the commands to view the base, ours, and theirs versions of the file straight from the index, and name the mechanism that makes this possible.',
+ c:[{l:'git show :1:path — base (stage 1)',t:[':1:','stage 1','stage one']},
+    {l:'git show :2:path — ours (stage 2)',t:[':2:','stage 2','stage two']},
+    {l:'git show :3:path — theirs (stage 3)',t:[':3:','stage 3','stage three']},
+    {l:'unmerged index stages hold all three blob versions during conflict',t:['index','unmerged','stages','blob','three versions']}],
+ m:`During a conflict the index holds the file in three numbered stages instead of one entry:
+- git show :1:Silmulator/docs/learning/PROGRESS.md   → stage 1, the BASE (merge-base version)
+- git show :2:Silmulator/docs/learning/PROGRESS.md   → stage 2, OURS (HEAD)
+- git show :3:Silmulator/docs/learning/PROGRESS.md   → stage 3, THEIRS (the branch being merged)
+The mechanism: an unmerged path keeps all three blobs staged simultaneously; git ls-files -u lists them. The working-tree file with markers is just a rendering of stages 2 and 3 (plus 1 under diff3) — the pristine inputs stay available in the index the whole time, which is also what mergetools read. Resolving and running git add collapses the three stages back to one.`
+},
