+  <p class="tagline">Why this matters: converging tonight's six-branch stack made <code>docs/learning/PROGRESS.md</code> collide twice — once <strong>loudly</strong> (a conflict block at 24f142b) and once <strong>silently</strong> (a clean auto-merge at f2b6fbf that produced two "Session 4" headings). Git merges lines, not meaning: an append-only log conflicts at its append anchor by construction, and a merge that satisfies git can still violate the file's invariants.</p>
